# EEG Attention Monitor
# SNN classifies attention state (focused vs. relaxed) from EEG alpha band power.
# High alpha → relaxed interneuron fires and suppresses output; Low alpha → output fires.

Define a network named eeg_attention with timestep 0.002.
# Network with 1 input, 3 LIF neurons, 3 linear transforms, 1 output.
# flow: input → sensor → actuator → output
#        sensor → interneuron → actuator (inhibitory suppression path)

# Layers:
Define an input port named input with shape (1,).
Define a LIF neuron named sensor with time constant 0.05, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 0.4.
Define a linear transformation named w_sensor_interneuron with weight matrix shape (35, 1) annotated with metadata weight_init equal to "xavier" annotated with metadata seed equal to 42.
Define a LIF neuron named interneuron with time constant 0.01, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 0.35.
Define a linear transformation named w_interneuron_actuator with weight matrix shape (1, 35).
# inhibitory connection (weight will be negative) — zero-initialised intentionally
Define a linear transformation named w_sensor_actuator with weight matrix shape (1, 1) annotated with metadata weight_init equal to "xavier" annotated with metadata seed equal to 43.
Define a LIF neuron named actuator with time constant 0.03, resistance 1.0, leak voltage 0.0, and firing threshold 0.6.
Define an output port named output with shape (1,).

# Connections:
input connects to sensor.
sensor connects to w_sensor_interneuron.
w_sensor_interneuron connects to interneuron.
interneuron connects to w_interneuron_actuator.
w_interneuron_actuator connects to actuator.
sensor connects to w_sensor_actuator.
w_sensor_actuator connects to actuator.
actuator connects to output.

# Note: thalamocortical transmission delay (10 ms) is dropped — not representable in NIR.
